<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ajaigarh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ajaygarh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ajaigarh is a hill fort and town in Panna district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on a flat-topped hill above the Ken river. It was one of the great strongholds of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandela-dynasty">Chandela dynasty</a>, which held out there after losing Kalinjar in 1203, and contains Chandela temples and inscriptions. From the 18th century it was the seat of the princely state of Ajaigarh.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ajaigarh.jpg" alt="Ajaigarh" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aminesh.aryan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajaygarh_Fort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
